      <data key="d3">"PROGRAM"</data>
      <data key="d4">"Corliss Archer aired on ABC from October 3, 1952, to June 26, 1953, and then returned to CBS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corliss Archer is a radio program from the Golden Age of Radio. It ran from January 7, 1943, to September 30, 1956."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corliss Archer is the character portrayed by Shirley Temple in Kiss and Tell."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corliss Archer is the title character in the radio program Meet Corliss Archer, played by Janet Waldo."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corliss Archer is the title character in “Meet Corliss Archer,” played by Janet Waldo."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corliss Archer was broadcast by NBC in 1948 as a summer replacement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Corliss Archer was created as CBS’s answer to the popular NBC program A Date with Judy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fewer than 24 episodes of Corliss Archer are known to exist, despite its long broadcast run."&lt;SEP&gt;"The radio program discussed in the text, also named in the title Meet Corliss Archer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70193bc69a5e8266573690f91b39c705&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5eaa2da9f0811b4525c4704d7ba4319f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-deab7907e4dda2d33cf5a38e7bc1df85</data>
