    <node id="&quot;CHARLES CRAFT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">entity</data>
      <data key="d3">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d4">"Charles Craft (May 9, 1902–September 19, 1968) was an English-born American film and television editor. He was born in Hampshire, England, and died in Los Angeles, California."&lt;SEP&gt;"Charles Craft began editing the television series based on Flipper, editing its first 28 episodes before retiring in 1966."&lt;SEP&gt;"Charles Craft edited 90 feature-length films over a 25-year period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Charles Craft entered the film industry in Hollywood in 1927."&lt;SEP&gt;"Charles Craft retired from editing in 1966."&lt;SEP&gt;"Charles Craft retired in 1966 after editing the first 28 episodes of the Flipper television series."&lt;SEP&gt;"Charles Craft shifted his professional focus from film editing to television in the early 1950s."&lt;SEP&gt;"Charles Craft was one of the main editors of Sea Hunt and edited over half of its episodes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Charles Craft worked on several television series during the 1950s."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b467e5adf53d4b410c6567550fb8881b</data>
